; Network-effect boundary for the reviewed Rust declarations a host
; selects.
;
; The protected declarations are not authored in this policy. They come
; from the reviewed declaration-selection document it imports, so the
; released policy ID runs unchanged for every repository and an
; unconfigured run fails activation instead of passing vacuously.
; Purity is never inferred from a function name, a file name, a comment, or an
; unqualified attribute.
;
; API choice: `std::net::TcpStream::connect`, written at arity one. It is an
; associated function of a standard-library type, so the Rust path resolver
; binds it from either spelling the language offers -- the verbatim
; `std::net::TcpStream::connect(addr)` or the one written segment
; `TcpStream::connect(addr)` a `use std::net::TcpStream;` declaration expands.
; `reqwest::blocking::get` would bind the same way, but it depends on a
; third-party crate being resolvable, so the standard-library identity is the
; smaller exact API. The written arity one disambiguates it from the generic
; `ToSocketAddrs` overloads the standard library offers at other arities.
;
; Activation
; ----------
; 1. Ship or install a reviewed semantic model for this language that declares
;    the concrete network API identity with the effect `bifrost.network_io`.
;    `semantic-packs/web-network/rust/bifrost.web-network-rust.json` is the
;    reviewed model for `std::net::TcpStream::connect`; place it under
;    `.bifrost/semantic-models/`.
; 2. Write the reviewed declaration selection to
;    `.bifrost/effect-boundaries/rust-network-io.rqlp`:
;      (declaration-selection-document
;        :schema-version 1
;        :language rust
;        :declarations [
;          (rql (enclosing-decl (function :name "total")))])
;    Each entry is one exact `enclosing-decl` selector of a function, method,
;    or class with an exact `:name`, optionally inside one exactly named
;    owner (`inside-decl`). The document admits no other constraint and no
;    nested file reference. A missing, empty, malformed, wrong-kind or
;    wrong-language document fails activation (`policy-validation-failed`),
;    and the imported selection is part of the run's `policy_hash`. A host
;    that scans untrusted repositories owns this path: it writes its reviewed
;    document there and never runs the repository's own copy.
; 3. Enable the policy by its ID; it is opt-in and never joins a default
;    run: `bifrost --policy-id
;    bifrost.effects.rust.selected-boundary-no-network-io --fail-on error`.
;
; The rule body is shared across languages; only the language label, the
; activated model, and the imported selection differ.
(policy
  :schema-version 1
  :id "bifrost.effects.rust.selected-boundary-no-network-io"
  :name "Selected Rust boundary reaches no network effect"
  :message "the selected Rust boundary reaches the declared network effect"
  :severity error
  :description "No explicitly selected Rust declaration may reach a declared network effect, directly or through workspace helpers. The effect is declared by a reviewed semantic model on the exact external API identity, never inferred from a function name, a file name, a comment, or an unqualified attribute. The protected declarations come from the reviewed declaration-selection document `.bifrost/effect-boundaries/rust-network-io.rqlp`; a missing or invalid document fails activation instead of passing."
  :help-uri "https://bifrost.brokk.ai/static-analysis-policies/#network-effect-boundary"
  :tags ["effects" "network" "boundary" "rust"]
  :analysis
    (analysis
      :type assertion
      ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
      ; Declaration selection: imported, never authored here. `effect` reads
      ; the procedure effects of exactly the declarations `selected` binds,
      ; so the two cannot drift apart and the policy derives no effect
      ; closure for a declaration it did not select.
      ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
      (bind :name selected
        :query (declaration-selection-file
          :path ".bifrost/effect-boundaries/rust-network-io.rqlp"
          :language rust))
      (bind :name effect
        :query (procedure-effects-of :binding selected))
      (join :left selected :right effect :on ((id procedure_id)))
      (group :name selected-boundary :by (selected.id)
        (aggregate :name network-effects :op count
          :where ((effect.effect_id eq "bifrost.network_io")
                  (effect.derivation eq declared))))
      (assert :group selected-boundary :value network-effects :cardinality (exactly 0))))
